
DEFINE CN1 as Unscrew pedals from bicycle
DEFINE CN2 as Comfortable to use with one hand
DEFINE FR1 as Fit 15 mm nut
DEFINE FR2 as Transmit sufficient torque
DEFINE FR3 as Fit between pedal and frame
COUPLE CN1 to FR1 because Common size for pedals
COUPLE CN1 to FR2 because Pedals must be screwed tight
COUPLE CN1 to FR3 because This is a narrow space
DEFINE FR4 as Handle fits human hand
DEFINE FR5 as Distribute loads with padding
COUPLE CN2 to FR4 because Handles must be designed to fit
COUPLE CN2 to FR5 because Padding is a common approach
DEFINE DP1 as Steel plate body
DEFINE DP2 as Plastic dipped handles
COUPLE FR1 to DP1 because Can be cut easily
COUPLE FR2 to DP1 because Steel is strong
COUPLE FR3 to DP1 because Plate can be made thin
COUPLE FR4 to DP1 because Easy to cut from plate
COUPLE FR5 to DP2 because Common padding method
DEFINE FR2.1 as Transmit >= 40 Nm
DEFINE DP1.1 as 5 mm thickness
COUPLE FR2.1 to DP1.1 because Sufficient bending strength
DEFINE FR3.1 as Fit within 10 mm gap
COUPLE FR3.1 to DP1.1 because Sufficient clearance
DEFINE PV1 as Cut from plate stock
DEFINE PV1.1 as Make on CNC mill
DEFINE PV2 as Purchase plastic dipping compound
COUPLE DP1.1 to PV1.1 because Milling possible
COUPLE DP2 to PV2 because COTS solution
ACCEPT PV1.1 because Ready for production
ACCEPT PV2 because Easily available
